Subject: [PATCH 34/38] docs: a README, CHANGELOG and NOTICE for the build
 repository

The build repository is generated, and every rdgen update force-pushes it,
so documentation committed there by hand is lost at the next update. These
files are new (upstream has none of them), so they never conflict with
upstream. .github/README.md, which GitHub shows ahead of upstream's root
README.md, says what the repository is, that it is not edited by hand, and
which secrets and variables it reads. CHANGELOG.md points at the installer's
changelog, and NOTICE credits rdgen and RustDesk.
