+# rdgen build repository
+
+[![License: GPL-3.0](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-GPL--3.0-blue)](../LICENSE)
+
+This private repository builds your custom RustDesk clients. rdgen, running in your
+[rustdesk-cortendesk-pve](https://github.com/rob-paprocki/rustdesk-cortendesk-pve) container, starts each build here
+as a workflow run, downloads the finished files, and then deletes the run and its artifacts. GitHub never connects to
+the container.
+
+**Don't edit this repository by hand.** It holds [upstream rdgen](https://github.com/bryangerlach/rdgen) with the
+installer's patch series applied, and the container's daily update replaces the whole branch with a force push.
+Anything committed here, merged Dependabot pull requests included, is gone after the next update, and until then a
+workflow that no longer matches the inputs rdgen sends makes builds fail. Change the patch series in the installer
+repository instead. Updates leave secrets and variables alone, because they live in the repository's settings.
+
+## Workflows
+
+| Workflow | Builds |
+|---|---|
+| `generator-windows.yml`, `generator-windows-x86.yml` | Windows clients (.exe and .msi) |
+| `generator-linux.yml` | Linux packages: .deb, .rpm, Arch, AppImage and Flatpak |
+| `generator-macos.yml` | macOS .dmg, for Intel, Apple Silicon or both |
+| `generator-android.yml` | Android .apk |
+| `fetch-encrypted-secrets.yml`, `bridge.yml` | Helper jobs that the builds call |
+
+## Settings
+
+Set these under **Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions**.
+
+| Name | Kind | Required | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `ZIP_PASSWORD` | secret | yes | Decrypts the build config. `rdgen-setup` sets it. |
+| `MACOS_P12_BASE64`, `MACOS_P12_PASSWORD` | secret | no | Signs Mac builds with your Developer ID certificate |
+| `APPLE_API_ISSUER_ID`, `APPLE_API_KEY_ID`, `APPLE_API_KEY_P8` | secret | no | Notarizes signed Mac builds |
+| `RDGEN_RUNNER_LINUX`, `RDGEN_RUNNER_LINUX_ARM`, `RDGEN_RUNNER_WINDOWS`, `RDGEN_RUNNER_MACOS_X86_64`, `RDGEN_RUNNER_MACOS_AARCH64` | variable | no | The label of a runner of your own; those jobs run there instead of on GitHub's machines |
+| `RDGEN_LINUX_DRM` | variable | no | `true` runs the Linux Wayland (DRM) job on your own Linux runner |
+
+[SETUP-PULL.md](../SETUP-PULL.md) has the full setup, including the two tokens and runners of your own.
+
+## Layout
+
+| Path | Contents |
+|---|---|
+| `README.md` | Upstream rdgen's README |
+| `SETUP-PULL.md` | Setup, tokens, runners, updates and what is protected |
+| `rdgenerator/` | The Django app and its tests |
+| `.github/workflows/` | The build workflows, generated by `tools/pullify.py` |
+| `tools/` | `pullify.py` and `rdgen-github-bootstrap` |
+| `deploy/` | systemd, OpenRC and nginx files |
+
+## License
+
+GPL-3.0, like upstream rdgen. [NOTICE](../NOTICE) credits rdgen and RustDesk, and [CHANGELOG.md](../CHANGELOG.md)
+says where changes are recorded.
